an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(4\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{9}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10}{7}\\times \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this product by swapping the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10}{7}\\times \\frac{9}{2} & =\\frac{10}{2}\\times \\frac{9}{7} \\\\  & =5\\times \\frac{9}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{45}{7}=6\\,\\text{R}3=6\\,\\frac{3}{7}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3e54fa1d-e140-5aab-8b59-8cf0883aae64"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3e54fa1d-e140-5aab-8b59-8cf0883aae64" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e54fa1d-e140-5aab-8b59-8cf0883aae64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f02f9f2b-912a-54fc-af54-7886155ad647" :answer-field/choices ["answer-459aa01e-a1de-59c7-a22e-0c0af77cdc21" "answer-9c889a63-ef4c-5a20-98b1-a165ccfce3be" "answer-1a9d135e-5c64-5722-a79d-9ab99644e1ae" "answer-88bc2fa6-4af5-5fcf-a326-665e84ae8461" "answer-f02f9f2b-912a-54fc-af54-7886155ad647"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-459aa01e-a1de-59c7-a22e-0c0af77cdc21" :answer/id #uuid "459aa01e-a1de-59c7-a22e-0c0af77cdc21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\frac{3}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c889a63-ef4c-5a20-98b1-a165ccfce3be" :answer/id #uuid "9c889a63-ef4c-5a20-98b1-a165ccfce3be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\,\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a9d135e-5c64-5722-a79d-9ab99644e1ae" :answer/id #uuid "1a9d135e-5c64-5722-a79d-9ab99644e1ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\frac{1}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88bc2fa6-4af5-5fcf-a326-665e84ae8461" :answer/id #uuid "88bc2fa6-4af5-5fcf-a326-665e84ae8461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f02f9f2b-912a-54fc-af54-7886155ad647" :answer/id #uuid "f02f9f2b-912a-54fc-af54-7886155ad647" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-867d7685-55ae-5d57-a541-e247084d254e" :question/id #uuid "867d7685-55ae-5d57-a541-e247084d254e" :question/math-academy-id "q-57157" :question/problem "$1\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\times 2\\,\\frac{1}{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{2}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{(1\\times 3)+2}{3}=\\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nWe also write  $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}\\times \\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this product by swapping the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}\\times \\frac{9}{4} & =\\frac{5}{4}\\times \\frac{9}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\times 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{4}=3\\,\\text{R}3=3\\,\\frac{3}{4}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cc7d59a3-fc09-5b10-beb2-e8114f4a5f9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cc7d59a3-fc09-5b10-beb2-e8114f4a5f9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc7d59a3-fc09-5b10-beb2-e8114f4a5f9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-00f80a56-583d-5f51-8b67-5d5f81a6737c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae06a46e-dae9-560e-a353-62ee5dbbdc1d" "answer-90b0eefc-85ce-5d28-bdee-d86ecf473d19" "answer-8a87e5d3-099b-54d6-a874-fe3ce664ebb6" "answer-d93976bd-1341-5ca9-8e28-f6b509d84f4c" "answer-00f80a56-583d-5f51-8b67-5d5f81a6737c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae06a46e-dae9-560e-a353-62ee5dbbdc1d" :answer/id #uuid "ae06a46e-dae9-560e-a353-62ee5dbbdc1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90b0eefc-85ce-5d28-bdee-d86ecf473d19" :answer/id #uuid "90b0eefc-85ce-5d28-bdee-d86ecf473d19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a87e5d3-099b-54d6-a874-fe3ce664ebb6" :answer/id #uuid "8a87e5d3-099b-54d6-a874-fe3ce664ebb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d93976bd-1341-5ca9-8e28-f6b509d84f4c" :answer/id #uuid "d93976bd-1341-5ca9-8e28-f6b509d84f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00f80a56-583d-5f51-8b67-5d5f81a6737c" :answer/id #uuid "00f80a56-583d-5f51-8b67-5d5f81a6737c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144084 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to multiply the following mixed numbers:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\dfrac 1 {3} \\times 1\\,\\dfrac 2{5}\n$$\n\nTo solve this problem, we can use the following three steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Convert both mixed numbers to improper fractions. \n\n- First, we write $1\\,\\dfrac 1 {3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\dfrac 1 {3}=\\dfrac{(3\\times 1)+1}{3}= \\dfrac43\n$$\n\n- We also write $1\\,\\dfrac25$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\dfrac25=\\dfrac{(5\\times 1)+2}{5}= \\dfrac75\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac43\\times\\dfrac75=  \\dfrac {4\\times 7} {3\\times 5} = \\dfrac{28}{15}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Simplify or convert back to a mixed number, if necessary:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{28}{15} = 1 \\, \\text{R} 13 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{13}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the answer is $1 \\, \\dfrac{13}{15}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143016 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
